@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16); [validated by: returns a required-property rejection without invoking the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L15)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- When valid input includes undeclared extra properties, `ToolRegistry.execute` passes the input through unchanged and invokes the executor exactly once ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L41)).
+- For a nested wrong-typed value, the rejection names its full property path and expected type without echoing the value ([validated by: names the full nested property path when a value has the wrong type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L106)).
+- When a property value is outside its declared `enum`, the rejection names the property and the enum constraint ([validated by: names the property and enum constraint when input is outside an enum](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L127)).
+- A rejected property value is omitted from both returned text and emitted log lines ([validated by: does not log or return a rejected property value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L148)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults.
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake ([validated by: throws for an unknown tool name without invoking an executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L34)).
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: static schemas compile once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L87)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules.
+- A function-valued tool definition is validated against the schema returned for each execution, even when successive calls return different schemas ([validated by: validates function-valued tools against the schema resolved on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L57)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
+- `processMessage` resolves after the provider receives a rejected tool call as a result and retries with corrected arguments ([validated by: returns an input rejection to the provider so it can retry with corrected arguments](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L402)).
+- The provider can retry after the rejection and the final result includes text from every model round ([validated by: joins the text of every round, not only the last](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L533)).
+- Once `maxToolRounds` is spent, the orchestrator stops asking the provider for additional tool calls ([validated by: stops asking for tools once maxToolRounds is spent](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L475)).
+- A client message that upserts a session entry is emitted with the entry's actual session index ([validated by: appends an upserted entry to the session and rewrites its index to match](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L503)).
